  "report": "# L002 recovery of a clustered ledger: COMPLETED\n\nSeeds: 17, 29, 43, 71, 101. Every seed must hold every coverage and falsifier rule.\n\n- seed 17: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 29: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 43: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 71: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 101: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n\n- mutation check: 32 of 32 killed\n\nLimitations: power loss is a fsync-honest crash-image model: bytes synced before the crash are intact and nothing else is promised; it is not a real power cut, and images exist for the new log and the anchor of the cutover and for a member's log, not for a member's state or snapshot file; the process-abort class is an in-process panic at a failpoint (the unwinding drops the handles; no destructor of the code under test writes); child processes that call abort() are not repeated from L001-v2; the durability probe sees file data pages only; a missing directory fsync is outside what it detects, and the model takes the directory fsync on trust; the Raft members return all their messages from one call, so the order of persisting and sending inside RaftNode::drain is not observable; the checked contract is that nothing a call returns promises a vote or an append that is not in the member's files and that a failed write returns no message; three in-process members on a deterministic router: no sockets, no election timer, no membership change, no real wire (ptr-cluster, ptr-net); recovery time is a count of heartbeat rounds, not a duration; RaftEngineLedger is not touched (L001-v2's stated limit and owner decision stand); synthetic seeded histories of 10 to 16 events; one process for the in-process arms, one machine profile.\n"
}
